 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Agent tools
+
+The sign-in and sign-up forms expose the `sign-in` and `sign-up` tools using
+the [WebMCP Declarative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api).
+Open `/devtools-times/signin` or `/devtools-times/signup` in a browser with
+WebMCP enabled to make the corresponding tool available to an agent.
+
+Both tools take required `username` and `password` parameters. Sign-up also
+declares the displayed password requirements: at least eight characters and a
+number. The user reviews the populated form and clicks Submit; these account
+tools do not opt into `toolautosubmit`.
+
+Submissions use the existing account APIs and return the displayed success or
+error message through `SubmitEvent.respondWith()`. Credentials and tokens are
+not included in tool results. Browsers without WebMCP retain the usual manual
+form behavior.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
